{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## RCA (runtime-confirmed) — foreign `stale-head` from the unscoped whole-HEAD currency read\n\n**Legitimacy: `defect`.** The unscoped whole-HEAD \"fail-safe\" currency arm violates its own\ncontract: it must decide whether the *reviewed code* has moved since review (anchored to the\nsigned gate-ref sha), but instead reads `git rev-parse HEAD` of whatever working tree the\nevaluator sits in and compares that against a gate-ref anchor.\n\n### Mechanism (proven at runtime, DEBUG-rebar-debug instrumentation)\n\n`compute_validity` unscoped arm, `src/rebar/llm/plan_review/attest.py:655-663`:\n```\nelif manifest_file_scope(auth_manifest) != \"none\":\n    head = signing.head_sha(_config.repo_root(repo_root))   # git rev-parse HEAD of a working tree\n    signed_head = _authoritative_head(attestation)          # for attested opcert = merged_log_commit = verified_at_sha = GATE-REF sha\n    if head == \"unknown\" or signed_head != head:\n        return _result(False, ..., \"stale-head\")\n```\nFor an **attested** opcert, `_authoritative_head` (attest.py:398-410) returns `merged_log_commit`,\nwhich `_opcert_signing.py:372` sets to `verified_at_sha` — the **gate-ref (origin/main) sha at\nreview time**. So the check compares a *gate-ref* sha against a *working-tree branch HEAD*. They\nmatch only by luck (a fetched main-tracking checkout). Any other tree — a feature-branch worktree,\nthe long-lived MCP server's own cwd, or a `git rev-parse HEAD` that walks UP out of a no-`.git`\nattested-snapshot dir into a foreign enclosing repo — yields a spurious, **foreign** `stale-head`.\n\nBecause both the gate-ref anchor and the foreign tree's HEAD are stable, the foreign value is\n**identical across invocations** (matches the ticket's two-reads-15-min-apart evidence: a\nstuck/foreign read, not a live race). origin/main having NOT moved is exactly why the review is\ngenuinely fresh yet still rejected.\n\n**Runtime evidence** (targeted repro, gate ref G unmoved, working tree diverged to feature F):\n```\ngate ref origin/main (G)          = 440a34c6fb8dc0c73bce0e7137cdf879d0aa4d17\nworking-tree HEAD    (F)          = 32a8985e892377fa31486441e31daeb254a07a47   (foreign to gate ref)\nsigned_head (_authoritative_head) = 440a34c6...   (== G, the signed gate-ref anchor)\nhead_sha read from repo_root      = .../repo   ->  returned 32a8985e...  (== F)\ncompute_validity verdict          = 'stale-head'  valid=False\nreason: attestation is stale (unscoped; signed at 440a34c6..., HEAD is 32a8985e...)\n```\nConfirmed: the currency check certified against G, then read the *working tree* F, not the gate\nref — a false `stale-head` while G is unmoved.\n\n### Root cause / attribution (`caused_by`, date-tested)\n\n- `3040aa0c` (2026-06-24, epic `boil-golem-veto` S1) introduced this unscoped whole-HEAD check.\n  It was **correct then**: pre-attested-snapshots, the *signed* side was also the working-tree\n  `head_sha`, so both sides were the same tree — symmetric, no defect.\n- **`ill-hazel-probe` (`30b3-b001-4ee2-43d2`, epic `raze-vet-ditch` S4, 2026-06-27)** made\n  `verified_at_sha` the signed anchor — a **gate-ref sha** — for attested opcerts, but did **not**\n  update this unscoped whole-HEAD *current* read to resolve the gate ref. That change **created\n  the asymmetry** (gate-ref signed side vs working-tree current side). → **true origin / unmet\n  obligation.** `0c1d0c18` (2026-07-21) only re-touched adjacent lines (pin-validity) — a carrier,\n  not the origin.\n- Siblings `piney-gold-day` (S4b) / `72d9` / `505d` fixed the **scoped** path to re-hash at the\n  current gate ref (ADR 0002, `gate_ref_hash_basis`, fail-closed) but never migrated the\n  **unscoped** whole-HEAD path — this is the missed consumer. (505d is DISTINCT: it fixes the\n  scoped path failing OPEN; this bug is the unscoped path failing CLOSED with a foreign value.)\n\n### Fix scope (respects the ticket non-goal)\n\nMirror the already-shipped scoped-path pattern: in the unscoped whole-HEAD arm, when the manifest\ncarries a `verified_at_sha` (attested), resolve the **current gate-ref sha** locally\n(`resolve_ref(default_ref, repo_root, fetch=False)`) and compare to the signed `verified_at_sha`;\nfail **closed honestly** (\"cannot confirm gate ref\") if unresolvable — never a foreign value.\nLegacy opcerts with no `verified_at_sha` keep the `head_sha` read unchanged. This **preserves the\nwhole-HEAD invalidation granularity/semantics** (still whole-origin/main, still fails closed on a\ngenuinely moved gate ref) and corrects only the wrong VALUE read — squarely within the ticket's\ndeclared non-goal (do NOT change invalidation granularity)."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788046611816452001,"uuid":"0b430279-d474-4ef0-98aa-74a98ca1f1cc"}